In line with our expectations, we expect our team members to be passionate about their work, to act with honesty and integrity, and to have a healthy dose of enthusiasm. The desired skills for the Quality Control Employee are also:
*  At least MBO level of working and thinking;
* 2-3 years work experience as a Quality Control Employee in a food company;
* Flexibility: working in four overlapping shifts, with Saturdays occasionally forming part of the working week;
* Fluency in spoken and written English; Dutch is an advantage;
* Knowledge of HACCP and GFSI;
* Strong communication skills, persuasive and decisive;
* Works accurately and is proactive;
* You are proficient in Excel and Word.

The New Plant - At The New Plant we produce Beyond Meats plant-based protein products for customers in Europe, the middle East and parts of Africa. Beyond Meat has been partnering with McDonalds sinds 2021 and supplies the vegetarian patty for the McPlant. Within your team, you will be working alongside three Quality Control Employee, a Quality Control Supervisor and a Quality Control Manager, and you will collaborate with two Quality Assurance Assistants.

CE-qualified driver 
 Nederland 
 € 2.893 - € 3.520 per month 
Do you enjoy being on the road and ensuring that deliveries arrive safely and on time? Then this role as a CE Driver could be just the thing for you. You'll be transporting chilled and frozen products to distribution centres, shops and wholesalers in the Netherlands and the Benelux. You'll work to a clear schedule and have frequent contact with customers and colleagues. No two days are the same, and you'll be a vital link in the transport process. 
 What are you going to do? 
As a CE-qualified driver, you'll ensure that products are delivered safely, in good condition and on schedule. 
• You will transport chilled and frozen products to customers in the Netherlands; 
• You will check pallets, consignment notes and other documents; 
• You will load, transport and unload goods in accordance with the applicable guidelines; 
• You'll liaise with the planning department in the event of any changes en route; 
• You'll complete the administrative tasks at the end of the day. 
 Who are you? 
As a CE driver, you work with precision and take responsibility for ensuring deliveries are carried out correctly. 
• You hold a CE driving licence; 
• You have a valid Code 95 certificate; 
• You have a valid driver card; 
• You speak Dutch or English; 
• You are motivated and work with care. 
 What do we offer? 
As a CE-licensed driver, you'll have a varied role within a stable organisation. 
• A gross monthly salary of between €2,893 and €3,520; 
• A contract with the prospect of permanent employment; 
• Travel allowance of €0.23 per kilometre in accordance with the collective labour agreement (maximum 35 km one way, excluding the first 10 km); 
• Access to an online learning platform and in-house Code 95 training courses; 
• Option to stay overnight during journeys if required. 
